-- PCC2: homogeneous coordinate support and signed complementation.
--
-- Informal proof. We work over a commutative ring R whose equality types
-- are propositions. The recursive representation is used explicitly:
-- Index 0 is the singleton and Index(n+1) is Index n + Index n;
-- Ext 0 is R and Ext(n+1) is Ext n * Ext n. The branches inl and inr
-- mean that the last basis vector is absent or present. Its presence
-- increases count by one. Coefficients, basis vectors, addition, negation,
-- scaling, alpha, star, and multiplication have the recursive clauses
-- specified below. Opening Ext or Index in these arguments only decodes
-- these two representations. Identifying the ring's sethood with isSet
-- unfolds that predicate; it supplies no algebraic equality.
-- The first/second accessors come from ExteriorModel. We explicitly
-- reopen their component clauses during these inductions, then lock
-- them again; there are no local copies of the model projections.
--
-- complement interchanges absence and presence at every position.
-- complement-invol follows by induction and congruence of inl/inr.
-- count-complement follows by the same induction: the inl clause uses
-- p+(q+1)=(p+q)+1 and the inr clause uses (p+1)+q=(p+q)+1.
--
-- top-prop is singleton elimination; prod-prop uses the named proposition
-- theorem for dependent pairs. For deg-prop open the degree predicate:
-- Deg 0 0 x is the singleton, Deg 0 (p+1) x is x=0,
-- Deg(n+1)0(x0,x1) is Deg n 0 x0 together with x1=0, and
-- Deg(n+1)(p+1)(x0,x1) is Deg n(p+1)x0 together with Deg n p x1.
-- These clauses are implemented by Deg's helpers deg0 and shift. The
-- induction hypothesis, sethood of R, and the named sethood of Ext n
-- show each factor is a proposition; prod-prop finishes.
--
-- Support means that coeff x i=0 whenever count i differs from p;
-- here Not P means P implies the empty type. coeff-support is induction
-- on n and p using precisely the degree clauses above, the coefficient
-- projections, and the clauses for count. At p=0 the inr coordinate is
-- zero because the second component is zero; coeff-zero justifies that
-- last step. At successor p the inr case reflects successor equality.
-- Conversely support-degree applies the induction hypothesis to the inl
-- and inr coordinates. At degree zero all inr coordinates vanish since
-- a successor is not zero; coordinate extensionality gives x1=0.
-- This proves the exact coefficient characterisation of homogeneity.
--
-- coeff-neg follows by the componentwise definition of eneg. twist i a
-- negates a once per position present in i. twist-mul follows by induction
-- from the named ring rule (-a)b=-(ab). neg-square uses that rule, the
-- right-negation rule, and double negation. twist-square then follows by
-- induction. Define epsilon 0=1; adjoining an absent position preserves
-- epsilon, and adjoining a present position applies twist(complement i)
-- to epsilon i. epsilon-square follows from twist-square and 1*1=1.
--
-- alpha(x0,x1)=(alpha x0,-alpha x1). Opening this clause, coefficients,
-- and twist proves coeff-alpha by induction, using coeff-neg. Likewise
-- star(x0,x1)=(alpha(star x1),star x0). Its coefficient at complement i
-- is epsilon i times coeff x i: the absent case is the induction
-- hypothesis; the present case uses coeff-alpha, the hypothesis, and
-- twist-mul. This is coeff-star. The base case uses the named unit law.
--
-- neg-scale is the componentwise equation -(a*x)=(-a)*x, proved from
-- the named scalar ring rule. For alpha-basis-scale open the basis
-- clauses basis(inl i)=(basis i,0), basis(inr i)=(0,basis i), scaling,
-- alpha, and twist. The nonzero component is the induction hypothesis,
-- followed by neg-scale in the inr case. The zero component uses the
-- named facts scale(a,0)=0, alpha(0)=0, and -0=0, with the common
-- point 0 written in each chain. star-zero follows from star's recursive
-- clause and alpha-zero. Now star-basis follows by induction: inl moves
-- the basis to the second component; inr moves it to the first and
-- applies alpha-basis-scale. The zero components use star-zero and
-- escale-zero. This proves star(basis i)=epsilon i * basis(complement i).
--
-- For homogeneous multiplication we state the representation interfaces
-- once. The upstream first/second accessors name the two Ext components. deg-left, deg-right0,
-- and deg-rightS are projections of the degree clauses above, and
-- deg-pair0/deg-pairS assemble those clauses. mul-rec states once, by
-- reflexivity, multiplication's equation
-- (x0,x1)*(y0,y1)=(x0*y0,x0*y1+x1*alpha(y0)).
-- deg-mul is induction on n, splitting p and q. In dimension zero a
-- positive degree forces a zero factor, so use the named zero-product
-- laws. For q=0 use deg-mul0 and p+0=p. For p=0,q>0 the second term
-- x1*alpha(y0) vanishes because x1=0. Otherwise both summands have
-- degree p+q-1 by induction and deg-alpha; plus-suc identifies the
-- two ways to write that index. deg-add and deg-pairS assemble the
-- result, and deg-eq transports along the named mul-rec equation.
--
-- Finally top-vanish is induction using the degree clauses and top's
-- projection to the last component. At dimension zero a positive degree
-- is x=0; at degree zero in positive dimension the last component is
-- zero, so apply the existing top-zero lemma. Otherwise recurse on
-- the last component and reflect successor equality in the inequality
-- p!=n. top-product-vanish applies deg-mul and top-vanish by name.
-- deg-scale writes a*x as emb(a)*x by the named emb-mul lemma and
-- applies deg-mul, deg-emb, and 0+p=p (the zero clause of plus).
-- After these characterisations, twist, epsilon, and the component
-- accessors are opaque; complement is likewise opaque outside the file.
--
-- Degree preservation and the Cramer support restriction. Equality of
-- natural numbers is decided by recursion: zero differs from a successor,
-- and successors are equal exactly when their predecessors are equal.
-- Left cancellation of addition is induction on the common first
-- summand; right cancellation follows by commuting both sums first.
--
-- A finite sum of degree-q elements has degree q, by induction on the
-- binary subset index and deg-add. A linear map f carries degree p to
-- degree q provided it does so on each basis vector of size p. Indeed,
-- map-expansion writes f(x) as the sum of coeff_i(x)*f(basis_i).
-- If count_i=p, its term has degree q by the hypothesis and deg-scale.
-- Otherwise coeff-support says that its scalar is zero, so the term is
-- zero by the shared named algebra law zero-scale. Zero has every degree.
-- Sum the resulting degree proofs and transport along map-expansion.
-- This is map-degree. phi-degree applies it to the existing basis image
-- theorem image-degree; the degree index is transported by count_i=p.
--
-- star-basis-degree applies deg-scale to the complementary basis and
-- transports along star-basis, so star(basis_i) has degree count(i^c).
-- If x has degree p and y has degree count(i^c), their top product is
-- zero when count_i differs from p: if p+count(i^c)=n, comparing with
-- count_i+count(i^c)=n and cancelling the common right summand would
-- give count_i=p. Thus top-product-vanish applies. This is
-- top-complement-vanish. Finally phi-degree gives the same degree for
-- phi_A(star(basis_i)); applying the preceding result proves
-- cramer-coeff-zero, exactly the coefficient needed to restrict the
-- all-subset Cramer expansion to subsets of size p.
--
-- Different homogeneous degrees are orthogonal for dot. Write dot as
-- the sum of products of coefficients. At each index decide count_i=p.
-- If so, count_i cannot equal q when p differs from q, and the second
-- coefficient vanishes. Otherwise the first coefficient vanishes.
-- The named multiplication-zero laws kill each term. scalar-sum-zero
-- sums these zero terms by induction, using 0+0=0 at each binary node;
-- dot-degree-vanish combines it with dot-sum.
--
-- For p+r=n, count_i=p implies count(i^c)=r by left cancellation in
-- count_i+count(i^c)=n; conversely count(i^c)=r implies count_i=p by
-- right cancellation. These are complement-count and its reflection.
-- Apply map-degree to star, using its two named linearity laws and
-- star-basis-degree with this index equality, to obtain star-degree.
-- For the converse, coeff-star expresses the complementary coefficient
-- of star(x) as epsilon_i*coeff_i(x). Outside degree p the complementary
-- index cannot have degree r, by the reflected count equality, so that
-- product is zero. epsilon-cancel-zero multiplies it by epsilon_i again;
-- epsilon-square, associativity, the unit law, and multiplication by zero
-- give coeff_i(x)=0. support-degree yields star-degree-reflect. Finally
-- star(unstar y)=y transports the degree-r proof to star(unstar y),
-- and the reflected theorem proves unstar-degree.
--
-- The dot pairing restricted to degree p is nondegenerate. To compare
-- two degree-p elements it suffices, by coordinate extensionality, to
-- compare their coefficients at each basis vector. Decide count_i=p.
-- In the equal case transport basis-degree along that equality, use
-- the hypothesis that the two elements pair equally with every
-- degree-p vector, and apply dot-basis on both sides. In the unequal
-- case both coefficients are zero by coeff-support. This proves
-- homogeneous-dot-inj using only test vectors of the specified degree.
--
level l ; open Ring[l] ;
module Pr = Prelude[l] ;
module C = ExteriorCoordinates[l] ;
complement : (n : Nat) -> C.Index n -> C.Index n = split {
 zero -> \ i -> i ; suc n | r -> split { inl i -> inr (r i) ; inr i -> inl (r i) } } ;
complement-invol : (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) -> Id (C.Index n) (complement n (complement n i)) i = split {
 zero -> \ i -> refl i ; suc n | r -> split { inl i -> ap (\ j -> inl j) (r i) ; inr i -> ap (\ j -> inr j) (r i) } } ;
module DecNat {
 step (m n : Nat) : Plus (Id Nat m n) (Not (Id Nat m n)) -> Plus (Id Nat (suc m) (suc n)) (Not (Id Nat (suc m) (suc n))) = split {
  inl e -> inl (ap (\ k -> suc k) e) ;
  inr ne -> inr (\ e -> ne (suc-inj e)) } ;
 dec : (m n : Nat) -> Plus (Id Nat m n) (Not (Id Nat m n)) = split {
  zero -> split { zero -> inl (refl zero) ; suc n -> inr (zero-suc n) } ;
  suc m | r -> split { zero -> inr (suc-zero m) ; suc n -> step m n (r n) } } ;
} ;
plus-cancel-left : (a b c : Nat) -> Id Nat (plus a b) (plus a c) -> Id Nat b c = split {
 zero -> \ b c e -> e ; suc a | r -> \ b c e -> r b c (suc-inj e) } ;
plus-cancel-right (a b c : Nat) (e : Id Nat (plus a c) (plus b c)) : Id Nat a b =
 plus-cancel-left c a b (trans (plus-comm c a) (trans e (sym (plus-comm c b)))) ;
module Over (Rg : CRing) (setR : Pr.isSet Rg.R) {
 open Rg ; module L = RL[Rg] ;
 module EA = ExteriorAlgebra[l].Over[Rg,setR] ;
 module DG = ExteriorDegree[l].Over[Rg,setR] ;
 module CO = C.Over[Rg,setR] ;
 module DU = ExteriorDuality[l].Over[Rg,setR] ;
 module BA = ExteriorBasis[l].Over[Rg,setR] ;
 module DT = Determinant[l].Over[Rg,setR] ;
 open ExteriorModel[l].Over[Rg] ;
 transparent first ; transparent second ;
 top-prop : Pr.isProp Top = split { tt -> split { tt -> refl tt } } ;
 prod-prop (A B : U l) (pa : Pr.isProp A) (pb : Pr.isProp B) : Pr.isProp (A * B) =
  Pr.isProp-Sigma A (\ a -> B) pa (\ a -> pb) ;
 deg-prop : (n p : Nat) (x : Ext n) -> Pr.isProp (DG.Deg n p x) = split {
  zero -> split { zero -> \ x -> top-prop ; suc p -> \ x -> setR x z } ;
  suc n | r -> split {
   zero -> \ x -> prod-prop (DG.Deg n zero (first n x)) (Id (Ext n) (second n x) (ezero n)) (r zero (first n x)) (EA.set n (second n x) (ezero n)) ;
   suc p -> \ x -> prod-prop (DG.Deg n (suc p) (first n x)) (DG.Deg n p (second n x)) (r (suc p) (first n x)) (r p (second n x)) } } ;
 Support (n p : Nat) (x : Ext n) : U l =
  (i : C.Index n) -> Not (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p) -> Id R (CO.coeff n x i) z ;
 coeff-support : (n p : Nat) (x : Ext n) -> DG.Deg n p x -> Support n p x = split {
  zero -> split {
   zero -> \ x d i ne -> efq (ne (refl zero)) ;
   suc p -> \ x d i ne -> d } ;
  suc n | r -> split {
   zero -> \ x d -> split {
    inl i -> \ ne -> r zero (first n x) d.1 i ne ;
    inr i -> \ ne -> trans (ap (\ y -> CO.coeff n y i) d.2) (CO.coeff-zero n i) } ;
   suc p -> \ x d -> split {
    inl i -> \ ne -> r (suc p) (first n x) d.1 i ne ;
    inr i -> \ ne -> r p (second n x) d.2 i (\ e -> ne (ap (\ k -> suc k) e)) } } } ;
 support-degree : (n p : Nat) (x : Ext n) -> Support n p x -> DG.Deg n p x = split {
  zero -> split { zero -> \ x h -> tt ; suc p -> \ x h -> h tt (zero-suc p) } ;
  suc n | r -> split {
   zero -> \ x h -> (r zero (first n x) (\ i ne -> h (inl i) ne),
    CO.ext n (second n x) (ezero n) (\ i -> trans (h (inr i) (suc-zero (BA.count n i))) (sym (CO.coeff-zero n i)))) ;
   suc p -> \ x h -> (r (suc p) (first n x) (\ i ne -> h (inl i) ne),
    r p (second n x) (\ i ne -> h (inr i) (\ e -> ne (suc-inj e)))) } } ;
 count-complement : (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) -> Id Nat (plus (BA.count n i) (BA.count n (complement n i))) n = split {
  zero -> \ i -> refl zero ; suc n | r -> split {
   inl i -> trans (plus-suc (BA.count n i) (BA.count n (complement n i))) (ap (\ k -> suc k) (r i)) ;
   inr i -> ap (\ k -> suc k) (r i) } } ;
 coeff-neg : (n : Nat) (x : Ext n) (i : C.Index n) -> Id R (CO.coeff n (eneg n x) i) (neg (CO.coeff n x i)) = split {
  zero -> \ x i -> refl (neg x) ; suc n | r -> \ x -> split { inl i -> r (first n x) i ; inr i -> r (second n x) i } } ;
 -- twist i a applies one negation per selected coordinate of i.
 twist : (n : Nat) -> C.Index n -> R -> R = split {
  zero -> \ i a -> a ; suc n | r -> split { inl i -> r i ; inr i -> \ a -> neg (r i a) } } ;
 twist-mul : (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) (a b : R) -> Id R (twist n i (mul a b)) (mul (twist n i a) b) = split {
  zero -> \ i a b -> refl (mul a b) ; suc n | r -> split {
   inl i -> r i ; inr i -> \ a b -> trans (ap neg (r i a b)) (sym (L.neg-mul-left (twist n i a) b)) } } ;
 neg-square (a : R) : Id R (mul (neg a) (neg a)) (mul a a) =
  trans (L.neg-mul-left a (neg a)) (trans (ap neg (L.mul-neg a a)) (L.neg-neg (mul a a))) ;
 twist-square : (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) (a : R) -> Id R (mul (twist n i a) (twist n i a)) (mul a a) = split {
  zero -> \ i a -> refl (mul a a) ; suc n | r -> split {
   inl i -> r i ; inr i -> \ a -> trans (neg-square (twist n i a)) (r i a) } } ;
 epsilon : (n : Nat) -> C.Index n -> R = split {
  zero -> \ i -> o ; suc n | r -> split { inl i -> r i ; inr i -> twist n (complement n i) (r i) } } ;
 epsilon-square : (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) -> Id R (mul (epsilon n i) (epsilon n i)) o = split {
  zero -> \ i -> mulO o ; suc n | r -> split {
   inl i -> r i ; inr i -> trans (twist-square n (complement n i) (epsilon n i)) (r i) } } ;
 coeff-alpha : (n : Nat) (x : Ext n) (i : C.Index n) -> Id R (CO.coeff n (alpha n x) i) (twist n i (CO.coeff n x i)) = split {
  zero -> \ x i -> refl x ; suc n | r -> \ x -> split {
   inl i -> r (first n x) i ; inr i -> trans (coeff-neg n (alpha n (second n x)) i) (ap neg (r (second n x) i)) } } ;
 coeff-star : (n : Nat) (x : Ext n) (i : C.Index n) ->
  Id R (CO.coeff n (DU.star n x) (complement n i)) (mul (epsilon n i) (CO.coeff n x i)) = split {
  zero -> \ x i -> sym (L.one-left x) ; suc n | r -> \ x -> split {
   inl i -> r (first n x) i ; inr i -> trans (coeff-alpha n (DU.star n (second n x)) (complement n i))
    (trans (ap (twist n (complement n i)) (r (second n x) i))
     (twist-mul n (complement n i) (epsilon n i) (CO.coeff n (second n x) i))) } } ;
 neg-scale : (n : Nat) (a : R) (x : Ext n) -> Id (Ext n) (eneg n (escale n a x)) (escale n (neg a) x) = split {
  zero -> \ a x -> sym (L.neg-mul-left a x) ;
  suc n | r -> \ a x -> ExteriorAlgebra[l].pair-eq (r a (first n x)) (r a (second n x)) } ;
 alpha-basis-scale : (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) (a : R) ->
  Id (Ext n) (alpha n (escale n a (CO.basis n i))) (escale n (twist n i a) (CO.basis n i)) = split {
  zero -> \ i a -> refl (mul a o) ; suc n | r -> split {
   inl i -> \ a -> ExteriorAlgebra[l].pair-eq (r i a)
    (trans (ap (\ x -> eneg n (alpha n x)) (EA.escale-zero n a))
     (trans (ap (eneg n) (EA.alpha-zero n))
      (trans EA.At[n].G.neg-zero (sym (EA.escale-zero n (twist n i a)))))) ;
   inr i -> \ a -> ExteriorAlgebra[l].pair-eq
    (trans (ap (alpha n) (EA.escale-zero n a))
     (trans (EA.alpha-zero n) (sym (EA.escale-zero n (neg (twist n i a))))))
    (trans (ap (eneg n) (r i a)) (neg-scale n (twist n i a) (CO.basis n i))) } } ;
 star-zero : (n : Nat) -> Id (Ext n) (DU.star n (ezero n)) (ezero n) = split {
  zero -> refl z ; suc n | r -> ExteriorAlgebra[l].pair-eq (trans (ap (alpha n) r) (EA.alpha-zero n)) r } ;
 star-basis : (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) ->
  Id (Ext n) (DU.star n (CO.basis n i)) (escale n (epsilon n i) (CO.basis n (complement n i))) = split {
  zero -> \ i -> sym (mulO o) ; suc n | r -> split {
   inl i -> ExteriorAlgebra[l].pair-eq
    (trans (ap (alpha n) (star-zero n))
     (trans (EA.alpha-zero n) (sym (EA.escale-zero n (epsilon n i))))) (r i) ;
   inr i -> ExteriorAlgebra[l].pair-eq (trans (ap (alpha n) (r i)) (alpha-basis-scale n (complement n i) (epsilon n i)))
    (trans (star-zero n) (sym (EA.escale-zero n (twist n (complement n i) (epsilon n i))))) } } ;
 -- Named interfaces for the two clauses of the degree predicate and
 -- the recursive multiplication equation, used below by their names.
 deg-left (n p : Nat) (x : Ext (suc n)) (d : DG.Deg (suc n) p x) : DG.Deg n p (first n x) = d.1 ;
 deg-right0 (n : Nat) (x : Ext (suc n)) (d : DG.Deg (suc n) zero x) : Id (Ext n) (second n x) (ezero n) = d.2 ;
 deg-rightS (n p : Nat) (x : Ext (suc n)) (d : DG.Deg (suc n) (suc p) x) : DG.Deg n p (second n x) = d.2 ;
 deg-pair0 (n : Nat) (x y : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n zero x) (dy : Id (Ext n) y (ezero n)) :
  DG.Deg (suc n) zero (x,y) = (dx,dy) ;
 deg-pairS (n p : Nat) (x y : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n (suc p) x) (dy : DG.Deg n p y) :
  DG.Deg (suc n) (suc p) (x,y) = (dx,dy) ;
 mul-rec (n : Nat) (x y : Ext (suc n)) : Id (Ext (suc n)) (emul (suc n) x y)
  (emul n (first n x) (first n y),eadd n (emul n (first n x) (second n y)) (emul n (second n x) (alpha n (first n y)))) = refl (emul (suc n) x y) ;
 deg-mul : (n p q : Nat) (x y : Ext n) -> DG.Deg n p x -> DG.Deg n q y -> DG.Deg n (plus p q) (emul n x y) = split {
  zero -> split {
   zero -> split { zero -> \ x y dx dy -> tt ; suc q -> \ x y dx dy -> trans (ap (mul x) dy) (L.mul-zero x) } ;
   suc p -> \ q x y dx dy -> trans (ap (\ t -> mul t y) dx) (L.zero-mul y) } ;
  suc n | r -> split {
   zero -> split {
    zero -> \ x y dx dy -> DG.deg-mul0 (suc n) zero x y dx dy ;
    suc q -> \ x y dx dy -> DG.deg-eq (suc n) (suc q) (mul-rec n x y)
     (deg-pairS n q (emul n (first n x) (first n y)) (eadd n (emul n (first n x) (second n y)) (emul n (second n x) (alpha n (first n y))))
      (r zero (suc q) (first n x) (first n y) (deg-left n zero x dx) (deg-left n (suc q) y dy))
      (DG.deg-add n q (emul n (first n x) (second n y)) (emul n (second n x) (alpha n (first n y)))
       (r zero q (first n x) (second n y) (deg-left n zero x dx) (deg-rightS n q y dy))
       (DG.deg-eq n q (trans (ap (\ t -> emul n t (alpha n (first n y))) (deg-right0 n x dx)) (EA.mul-zero-l n (alpha n (first n y)))) (DG.deg-zero n q)))) } ;
   suc p -> split {
    zero -> \ x y dx dy -> subst (\ k -> DG.Deg (suc n) k (emul (suc n) x y)) (sym (plus-zero (suc p))) (DG.deg-mul0 (suc n) (suc p) x y dx dy) ;
    suc q -> \ x y dx dy -> DG.deg-eq (suc n) (suc (plus p (suc q))) (mul-rec n x y)
     (deg-pairS n (plus p (suc q)) (emul n (first n x) (first n y)) (eadd n (emul n (first n x) (second n y)) (emul n (second n x) (alpha n (first n y))))
      (r (suc p) (suc q) (first n x) (first n y) (deg-left n (suc p) x dx) (deg-left n (suc q) y dy))
      (DG.deg-add n (plus p (suc q)) (emul n (first n x) (second n y)) (emul n (second n x) (alpha n (first n y)))
       (subst (\ k -> DG.Deg n k (emul n (first n x) (second n y))) (sym (plus-suc p q))
        (r (suc p) q (first n x) (second n y) (deg-left n (suc p) x dx) (deg-rightS n q y dy)))
       (r p (suc q) (second n x) (alpha n (first n y)) (deg-rightS n p x dx) (DG.deg-alpha n (suc q) (first n y) (deg-left n (suc q) y dy))))) } } } ;
 top-vanish : (n p : Nat) (x : Ext n) -> DG.Deg n p x -> Not (Id Nat p n) -> Id R (top n x) z = split {
  zero -> split { zero -> \ x d ne -> efq (ne (refl zero)) ; suc p -> \ x d ne -> d } ;
  suc n | r -> split {
   zero -> \ x d ne -> trans (ap (top n) d.2) (Adjugate[l].Over[Rg,setR].top-zero n) ;
   suc p -> \ x d ne -> r p (second n x) d.2 (\ e -> ne (ap (\ k -> suc k) e)) } } ;
 top-product-vanish (n p q : Nat) (x y : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) (dy : DG.Deg n q y)
  (ne : Not (Id Nat (plus p q) n)) : Id R (top n (emul n x y)) z =
  top-vanish n (plus p q) (emul n x y) (deg-mul n p q x y dx dy) ne ;
 deg-scale (n p : Nat) (a : R) (x : Ext n) (d : DG.Deg n p x) : DG.Deg n p (escale n a x) =
  DG.deg-eq n p (sym (EA.emb-mul n a x)) (deg-mul n zero p (emb n a) x (DG.deg-emb n a) d) ;
 sum-degree (m p : Nat) : (n : Nat) (u : C.Index n -> Ext m) -> ((i : C.Index n) -> DG.Deg m p (u i)) ->
  DG.Deg m p (CO.ES[m].SumE.sum n u) = split {
  zero -> \ u d -> d tt ;
  suc n | r -> \ u d -> DG.deg-add m p
   (CO.ES[m].SumE.sum n (\ i -> u (inl i))) (CO.ES[m].SumE.sum n (\ i -> u (inr i)))
   (r (\ i -> u (inl i)) (\ i -> d (inl i))) (r (\ i -> u (inr i)) (\ i -> d (inr i))) } ;
 module MapDegree (n m p q : Nat) (f : Ext n -> Ext m) (hf : CO.LinearMap n m f)
  (hb : (i : C.Index n) -> Id Nat (BA.count n i) p -> DG.Deg m q (f (CO.basis n i)))
  (x : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) {
  term (i : C.Index n) : Plus (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p) (Not (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p)) ->
   DG.Deg m q (escale m (CO.coeff n x i) (f (CO.basis n i))) = split {
   inl e -> deg-scale m q (CO.coeff n x i) (f (CO.basis n i)) (hb i e) ;
   inr ne -> DG.deg-eq m q
    (trans (ap (\ a -> escale m a (f (CO.basis n i))) (coeff-support n p x dx i ne))
     (EA.zero-scale m (f (CO.basis n i)))) (DG.deg-zero m q) } ;
  result : DG.Deg m q (f x) = DG.deg-eq m q (CO.map-expansion n m f hf x)
   (sum-degree m q n (\ i -> escale m (CO.coeff n x i) (f (CO.basis n i)))
    (\ i -> term i (DecNat.dec (BA.count n i) p))) ;
  opaque term ; opaque result ;
 } ;
 map-degree (n m p q : Nat) (f : Ext n -> Ext m) (hf : CO.LinearMap n m f)
  (hb : (i : C.Index n) -> Id Nat (BA.count n i) p -> DG.Deg m q (f (CO.basis n i)))
  (x : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) : DG.Deg m q (f x) = MapDegree[n,m,p,q,f,hf,hb,x,dx].result ;
 phi-degree (n : Nat) (A : DT.Mat n) (p : Nat) (x : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) : DG.Deg n p (DT.Map[n,A].value x) =
  map-degree n n p p DT.Map[n,A].value (DT.Map[n,A].value-add,DT.Map[n,A].value-scale)
   (\ i e -> subst (\ k -> DG.Deg n k (DT.Map[n,A].value (CO.basis n i))) e (BA.image-degree n A i)) x dx ;
 star-basis-degree (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) : DG.Deg n (BA.count n (complement n i)) (DU.star n (CO.basis n i)) =
  DG.deg-eq n (BA.count n (complement n i)) (star-basis n i)
   (deg-scale n (BA.count n (complement n i)) (epsilon n i) (CO.basis n (complement n i)) (BA.basis-degree n (complement n i))) ;
 top-complement-vanish (n p : Nat) (x : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) (i : C.Index n)
  (y : Ext n) (dy : DG.Deg n (BA.count n (complement n i)) y) (ne : Not (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p)) :
  Id R (top n (emul n x y)) z =
  top-product-vanish n p (BA.count n (complement n i)) x y dx dy
   (\ e -> ne (plus-cancel-right (BA.count n i) p (BA.count n (complement n i)) (trans (count-complement n i) (sym e)))) ;
 cramer-coeff-zero (n : Nat) (A : DT.Mat n) (p : Nat) (x : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x)
  (i : C.Index n) (ne : Not (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p)) :
  Id R (top n (emul n x (DT.Map[n,A].value (DU.star n (CO.basis n i))))) z =
  top-complement-vanish n p x dx i (DT.Map[n,A].value (DU.star n (CO.basis n i)))
   (phi-degree n A (BA.count n (complement n i)) (DU.star n (CO.basis n i)) (star-basis-degree n i)) ne ;
 scalar-sum-zero : (n : Nat) (f : C.Index n -> R) -> ((i : C.Index n) -> Id R (f i) z) -> Id R (CO.S.sum n f) z = split {
  zero -> \ f h -> h tt ;
  suc n | r -> \ f h -> trans
   (DU.cong (r (\ i -> f (inl i)) (\ i -> h (inl i))) (r (\ i -> f (inr i)) (\ i -> h (inr i)))) (addZ z) } ;
 module DotDegree (n p q : Nat) (x y : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) (dy : DG.Deg n q y) (ne : Not (Id Nat p q)) {
  term (i : C.Index n) : Plus (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p) (Not (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p)) ->
   Id R (mul (CO.coeff n x i) (CO.coeff n y i)) z = split {
   inl e -> trans (ap (mul (CO.coeff n x i)) (coeff-support n q y dy i (\ f -> ne (trans (sym e) f)))) (L.mul-zero (CO.coeff n x i)) ;
   inr e -> trans (ap (\ a -> mul a (CO.coeff n y i)) (coeff-support n p x dx i e)) (L.zero-mul (CO.coeff n y i)) } ;
  result : Id R (DU.dot n x y) z = trans (CO.dot-sum n x y)
   (scalar-sum-zero n (\ i -> mul (CO.coeff n x i) (CO.coeff n y i)) (\ i -> term i (DecNat.dec (BA.count n i) p))) ;
  opaque term ; opaque result ;
 } ;
 dot-degree-vanish (n p q : Nat) (x y : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) (dy : DG.Deg n q y) (ne : Not (Id Nat p q)) :
  Id R (DU.dot n x y) z = DotDegree[n,p,q,x,y,dx,dy,ne].result ;
 complement-count (n p r : Nat) (i : C.Index n) (e : Id Nat (BA.count n i) p) (h : Id Nat (plus p r) n) :
  Id Nat (BA.count n (complement n i)) r =
  plus-cancel-left p (BA.count n (complement n i)) r
   (trans (subst (\ k -> Id Nat (plus k (BA.count n (complement n i))) n) e (count-complement n i)) (sym h)) ;
 complement-count-reflect (n p r : Nat) (i : C.Index n) (e : Id Nat (BA.count n (complement n i)) r) (h : Id Nat (plus p r) n) :
  Id Nat (BA.count n i) p =
  plus-cancel-right (BA.count n i) p r
   (trans (subst (\ k -> Id Nat (plus (BA.count n i) k) n) e (count-complement n i)) (sym h)) ;
 star-degree (n p r : Nat) (x : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) (h : Id Nat (plus p r) n) : DG.Deg n r (DU.star n x) =
  map-degree n n p r (DU.star n) (DU.star-add n,DU.star-scale n)
   (\ i e -> subst (\ k -> DG.Deg n k (DU.star n (CO.basis n i))) (complement-count n p r i e h) (star-basis-degree n i)) x dx ;
 epsilon-cancel-zero (n : Nat) (i : C.Index n) (a : R) (e : Id R (mul (epsilon n i) a) z) : Id R a z =
  calc R { a =< sym (L.one-left a) > mul o a
   =< ap (\ s -> mul s a) (sym (epsilon-square n i)) > mul (mul (epsilon n i) (epsilon n i)) a
   =< sym (mulA (epsilon n i) (epsilon n i) a) > mul (epsilon n i) (mul (epsilon n i) a)
   =< ap (mul (epsilon n i)) e > mul (epsilon n i) z
   =< L.mul-zero (epsilon n i) > z } ;
 star-degree-reflect (n p r : Nat) (x : Ext n) (d : DG.Deg n r (DU.star n x)) (h : Id Nat (plus p r) n) : DG.Deg n p x =
  support-degree n p x (\ i ne -> epsilon-cancel-zero n i (CO.coeff n x i)
   (trans (sym (coeff-star n x i))
    (coeff-support n r (DU.star n x) d (complement n i) (\ e -> ne (complement-count-reflect n p r i e h))))) ;
 unstar-degree (n p r : Nat) (y : Ext n) (dy : DG.Deg n r y) (h : Id Nat (plus p r) n) : DG.Deg n p (DU.unstar n y) =
  star-degree-reflect n p r (DU.unstar n y) (DG.deg-eq n r (DU.star-unstar n y) dy) h ;
 homogeneous-dot-inj (n p : Nat) (x y : Ext n) (dx : DG.Deg n p x) (dy : DG.Deg n p y)
  (h : (w : Ext n) -> DG.Deg n p w -> Id R (DU.dot n x w) (DU.dot n y w)) : Id (Ext n) x y =
  CO.ext n x y (\ i -> term i (DecNat.dec (BA.count n i) p))
  where {
   term (i : C.Index n) : Plus (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p) (Not (Id Nat (BA.count n i) p)) ->
    Id R (CO.coeff n x i) (CO.coeff n y i) = split {
    inl e -> trans (sym (CO.dot-basis n x i))
     (trans (h (CO.basis n i) (subst (\ k -> DG.Deg n k (CO.basis n i)) e (BA.basis-degree n i))) (CO.dot-basis n y i)) ;
    inr ne -> trans (coeff-support n p x dx i ne) (sym (coeff-support n p y dy i ne)) } ;
  } ;
 opaque homogeneous-dot-inj ;
 opaque complement-count ; opaque complement-count-reflect ;
 opaque star-degree ; opaque epsilon-cancel-zero ; opaque star-degree-reflect ; opaque unstar-degree ;
 opaque scalar-sum-zero ; opaque dot-degree-vanish ;
 opaque sum-degree ; opaque map-degree ; opaque phi-degree ;
 opaque star-basis-degree ; opaque top-complement-vanish ; opaque cramer-coeff-zero ;
 opaque twist ; opaque epsilon ; opaque first ; opaque second ;
} ;
opaque complement ;
